Verify that two computers can speak to each other.
Used 'ping [IP address of computer B]' from command prompt, from computer A [host].
Got 'timed out', repeatedly.  
Destination PC is safely ignoring my ping because the Windows Firewall blocks inbound IPv6 echo requests by default.

To fix this, I need to tell the destination computer's firewall that it is allowed to respond to IPv6 pings.

In CP I ran:   
netsh advfirewall firewall add rule name="Allow IPv6 Inbound Ping" dir=in action=allow protocol=icmpv6 profile=private
Response: Ok

Go to host computer to ping destination IPv6 address
